{"t": 1794116015.8409917, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_push_files", "args": {"branch": "eng-91", "files": [{"content": "def deprecation_headers(sunset_date: str) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Return the deprecation headers for a v1 endpoint.\n\n    See the \"API guidelines\" page in Notion (section Deprecation):\n        Deprecation: true\n        Sunset: <HTTP-date>\n        Link: <https://developer.acme.example/migrate>; rel=\"deprecation\"\n\n    ``sunset_date`` must be the HTTP-date the endpoint will be removed on.\n    \"\"\"\n    return {\n        \"Deprecation\": \"true\",\n        \"Sunset\": sunset_date,\n        \"Link\": '<https://developer.acme.example/migrate>; rel=\"deprecation\"',\n    }\n", "path": "api/headers.py"}], "message": "ENG-91: add deprecation headers helper for v1 endpoints", "owner": "acme", "repo": "public-api"}, "ok": true}
{"t": 1794116020.991356, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_create_pull_request", "args": {"base": "main", "body": "Implements `api.headers.deprecation_headers(sunset_date)` for the v1 endpoints, per the Deprecation section of the \"API guidelines\" page in Notion.\n\nThe helper returns the three headers required by the guidelines:\n\n- `Deprecation: true`\n- `Sunset: <HTTP-date>` (value supplied by the caller)\n- `Link: <https://developer.acme.example/migrate>; rel=\"deprecation\"`\n\nLinear: ENG-91", "head": "eng-91", "owner": "acme", "repo": "public-api", "title": "ENG-91: Add deprecation headers to v1 endpoints"}, "ok": true}
